    Bug 1905616 - Use BrowserUtils.hrefAndLinkNodeForClickEvent() to check for link nodes inside shadow DOM. r=aleca


    If the clicked element is actually a complex shadow DOM, we currently do
    not see the actual clicked element but the retargeted one, and fail to
    extract the `href` attribute.

    This patch replaces our own `hRefForClickEvent()` function by the
    already existing `BrowserUtils.hrefAndLinkNodeForClickEvent()`, which
    correctly handles this case (and also XLINK).

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232156

